counterfactuals.output:
An apparatus for selectively actuating a jaw of a torch handle and for distributing gas through the torch handle, the apparatus comprising:

a torch handle body defining an internal gas passage extending between a gas inlet and a gas outlet, the gas outlet being in fluid communication with an exit orifice configured to discharge gas from the torch handle;

a jaw member movably coupled to the torch handle body and movable between an open position and a closed position relative to an opposing jaw portion;

a pneumatic actuator disposed at least partially within, or operatively coupled to, the torch handle body, the pneumatic actuator including an actuator chamber configured to receive pressurized gas;

a movable actuator element positioned in operative communication with the actuator chamber, the movable actuator element being displaced in response to admission of pressurized gas into the actuator chamber;

a linkage or force-transmitting member coupled between the movable actuator element and the jaw member, the linkage being configured to translate displacement of the movable actuator element into movement of the jaw member between the open and closed positions;

a valve arrangement in fluid communication with the gas inlet, the internal gas passage, and the actuator chamber, the valve arrangement being configured to selectively direct pressurized gas to the actuator chamber for pneumatic actuation of the jaw member and to direct gas through the internal gas passage toward the exit orifice; and

a return member configured to bias at least one of the movable actuator element and the jaw member toward a predetermined position when pneumatic pressure in the actuator chamber is reduced.

In operation, pressurized gas supplied to the gas inlet is distributed through the torch handle body to the exit orifice while at least a portion of the pressurized gas is selectively applied to the pneumatic actuator. Application of the pressurized gas to the actuator chamber displaces the movable actuator element, thereby causing the linkage to move the jaw member from one of the open and closed positions to the other of the open and closed positions. Venting or reduction of pressure within the actuator chamber permits the return member to move the jaw member back toward the predetermined position. The apparatus thereby provides both pneumatic opening and closing of the torch handle jaw and gas delivery through the handle to the exit orifice.
